# C5 review round 1 (Kimi: CHANGES; agy: CHANGES). Fix them on this branch.

HEAD is b5fff070 (axioms golden regenerated; all seven gates pass on concrete-ci-2). Do not edit scripts/proofs/axioms.golden. All rules of _review/BRIEF.md still apply (commit each piece after `nix develop -c timeout 1200 lake build ConcreteSpec` passes; do not push). Full reviewer texts: _review/kimi-r1.md, _review/agy-r1.md.

1. (agy 4, raised to major by the coordinator) Every transition wraps its result in `validate`, a run-time re-check of the whole invariant, so preservation (`f s = some t → WellFormed t`) holds by construction and an operation can be refused merely because the invariant would break. That is an enforced invariant, not a proved one, and it can hide spurious stuckness. Remove `validate` from the transitions: each operation checks only its own operational guard (conflict, status, identity), and prove preservation structurally from `WellFormed s`. Add progress lemmas: from a well-formed state, an operation whose stated guard holds succeeds. If some check must stay, name it as part of the rule and justify it in its doc comment.
2. (Kimi, major) Erasure is proved for one invocation of the `instrument` wrapper only. Prove it at the level of C1 executions: define the erased operand instance, prove the agreements for eval, test, life and allows, then prove step and multi-step simulation preserving events and the final classification (Steps / run). Do the same for the generative allocator wrapper, at least over a multi-step run.
3. (Kimi, major) Downward-only lending is not enforced: `reborrowAt` accepts any destination activation, so a caller loan can be reborrowed into activation 0 while activation 1 is current (an upward loan). Require the destination to be the current activation or the directly entered callee. Keep the arbitrary-destination helper private, add a refused upward-reborrow example, and prove a theorem stating the activation relationship.
4. (agy 1, major) `CallState.pending` has no invariant: `passDown` can duplicate a parameter; `.leave` with pending entries leaves dangling loan identities. Define `CallState.WellFormed` (own well-formed, parameters and loans in `pending` unique, and `pendingArgument = true` exactly for the loans in `pending`) and prove `passDown` and `callLife` preserve it, refusing the duplicate and stale cases.
5. (agy 2, major) Passing `&x`/`&mut x` from an owner requires borrow then passDown, and the caller's own loan stays active after the call returns, freezing `x`. Add the direct owner-to-callee form (a loan opened with `pendingArgument = true`, ended when the callee leaves), prove its preservation, and add an example where `x` is usable again after the call.
6. (Kimi, minor) The zero-size example cites `Hybrid.sizeof .unit = 0` as representation evidence, but Hybrid says unit has no representation and 0 is a sentinel. Use an explicit logical zero-size witness, or state the obligation without citing C4's sentinel.
7. (agy 3, minor) `Generative`: add `(s.dependencies.map Dependency.place).Nodup` to WellFormed, and document in Grant.lean's header that tying `Dependency.place` to the Own slot lifecycle is integration work (name the slice), not done here.
8. (Kimi nit) README O3: distinguish the old slice-1 `Entry` instrumentation, the C5 erasure results and anything still missing. (agy nit 5) `Grants.State`: add the defaults and `deriving DecidableEq, Repr` like the other states.

Final message: commits (SHA + one line), each finding fixed and how, new/changed theorem statements, anything left with a reason, QUESTIONS.

