[wip/spec-c5 8c071126] spec C5: prove generative preservation structurally with operational progress
 2 files changed, 270 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

codex
Generative preservation now builds without `validate`: fresh, depend, consume, release, reset and scope exit have structural proofs, plus progress lemmas and positive/bad-state examples.

A separate limitation affects finding 2: unconditional preservation of stuck classification is impossible with the current erasure wrapper. A use-after-move can be refused by instrumentation while its erased concrete read succeeds. I’ll record that distinction explicitly rather than claim full execution equivalence.
